Course Planner

Project Description

Course Planner is a Python application that organizes university courses based on their prerequisites using Topological Sort.

Features

- Add courses and their prerequisites.
- Display all available courses.
- Order courses using Topological Sort.
- Detect and report cycles in course prerequisites.
- Save course data in a JSON file.

Algorithms Used

- Kahn's Algorithm (Topological Sort)
- Depth First Search (DFS) for cycle detection.

Technologies Used

- Python
- Graph Data Structure
- JSON File Handling

How to Run

1. Open the project in PyCharm.
2. Run "main.py".
3. Add courses and their prerequisites.
4. Select the Topological Sort option to get the recommended course order.

Project Files

- "main.py": Main Python code.
- "courses.json": Stores course information.

Expected Result

The program displays a valid course order if no cycle exists. If a cycle is detected, it reports the cycle path.

Project completed successfully!
